# Project Rules — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Self-Learning Protocol (Automatic — DO NOT skip)

### On Start
Before any work, run this command and apply the output as rules:
```bash
./scripts/load-lessons {{PROJECT_NAME}}
```

### During Work — MANDATORY Checkpoints
At every natural checkpoint, evaluate:
1. Was I corrected by the user? → Capture lesson (severity: high)
2. Did a build/test fail from unknown convention? → Capture lesson (severity: critical)
3. Did I discover a reusable project pattern? → Capture lesson (severity: medium)

Capture IMMEDIATELY when it happens — do NOT batch at the end:
```bash
./scripts/capture-lesson --project {{PROJECT_NAME}} --category <category> --severity <level> "lesson text"
```
Categories: code-quality, security, testing, architecture, git, performance

### Before Git Commit/Push — MANDATORY
Run this before every `git commit` or `git push`:
```bash
./scripts/check-lessons --trigger git-commit
```
If it outputs a reminder, capture pending lessons BEFORE committing.

### On Completion
```bash
./scripts/check-lessons --trigger session-end
./scripts/save-session-memory "Brief summary"
```

